Replacing pinctrl_generic_set_state() with spacemit_pinctrl_set_state() to
force power-source before drive-strength ordering is a reasonable approach,
and reordering spacemit_pinconf_params[] alone wouldn't have been sufficient
since dev_read_prop() iteration order there still depends on array order,
not DT order - so the custom set_state() callback is the right fix.

A few questions on spacemit_pinctrl_apply_group():

- It reads "pinmux" from `config` via dev_read_size()/dev_read_u32_index(),
  but does this account for nodes using the generic "pins" + separate mux
  binding style instead of a packed "pinmux" array, or is this SoC's
  binding always a packed u32 pinmux list? If the driver only supports the
  latter, that's fine, just want to confirm it's intentional.

- spacemit_pinctrl_set_state() iterates `device_find_first_child()` /
  `device_find_next_child()` over `config` to also apply grouped
  sub-nodes. Is this recursing one level only, or could pinctrl groups be
  nested deeper in any real DT? If only one level is ever used, that's
  fine as-is.

- This changes the global set_state callback for the whole driver (used by
  both K1 and K3 per pinctrl-k1.c), not just K3 - can you confirm this was
  tested on K1 hardware too, since the series title says "k3-pinctrl" but
  the callback change is shared?
